        "problem": "Find $({f}^{-1})^{\u2032}(2)$ given the following table of values of functions $f(x)$ and ${f}^{\u2032}(x)$ at some points.\n\n| **$x$** | $f(x)$ | ${f}^{\u2032}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $0$ | $8$ |\n| $3$ | $2$ | $-5$ |\n\n$({f}^{-1})^{\u2032}(2)=$\n{{field-1}}",
        "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse is\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{\u2032}(x)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{\u2032}({f}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=2,$ we have\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{\u2032}(2)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{\u2032}({f}^{-1}(2))}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we obtain ${f}^{-1}(2)=3$ and ${f}^{\u2032}(3)=-5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{\u2032}(2) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{\u2032}({f}^{-1}(2))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{\u2032}(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-5)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
